# Local development only. Copy to .env; never commit .env.
DIREX_DB_OWNER_URL=postgres://direx_owner:direx_owner_dev@localhost:5435/direx
DIREX_DB_APP_URL=postgres://direx_app:direx_app_dev@localhost:5435/direx
# The one connection the app uses: tenant queries, Better Auth and the overdue-Action sweep.
# Optional: the same role through PgBouncer in transaction mode (`docker compose --profile
# pool up`). Unset, the pool tests are skipped and the concurrency test talks to Postgres.
# DIREX_DB_POOL_URL=postgres://direx_app:direx_app_dev@localhost:6435/direx
# Root key for the credential vault. Generated on first start into DIREX_DATA_DIR/master.key
# (default ~/.direx/master.key). Back that file up separately from the database: a backup
# without it restores no credential. Set one of these only to supply your own.
# DIREX_DATA_DIR
# DIREX_MASTER_KEY
# DIREX_MASTER_KEY_FILE
# Dev and test use a fixed auth secret, listen on 127.0.0.1 only, skip email confirmation for
# passwords, and log mail instead of sending it. Anywhere else the auth secret is generated in
# the vault on first start, a password needs a confirmed email address, and the API refuses to
# start without DIREX_MAIL_FROM below and: bun apps/api/src/secrets.ts set smtp.url
# The address people open: sign-in, invite and Mailbox connect links point here, and
# the Google redirect URIs start with it. Unset, it is the Vite dev server's address.
# DIREX_BASE_URL=http://localhost:5173
# Behind a reverse proxy, its address or range, comma-separated. Sign-in is rate limited per
# client address, and without this every person behind the proxy shares one limit. Unset, only
# the address a connection comes from is believed and X-Forwarded-For is ignored.
# DIREX_TRUSTED_PROXIES=127.0.0.1,10.0.0.0/8
# Days a sign-in lasts without use; each day of use pushes the end out, and every sign-in ends
# 90 days after it was made. A whole number from 2 to 90. Unset, 30. Self-hosted Direx only.
# DIREX_SESSION_DAYS=30
# DIREX_MAIL_FROM=Direx <signin@example.com>
# Where this server's source code is published; the sign-in page links to it. Unset, it is
# Direx's own repository, at the release in DIREX_VERSION when the Compose install set one. If you run a changed Direx, the AGPL asks you to offer your source
# to the people who use it: set this to where yours is.
# DIREX_SOURCE_URL=https://github.com/trydirex/direx
# Optional OAuth apps; each sign-in button appears only when its pair is set.
# DIREX_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
# Its client secret goes in the vault, typed by a person: bun apps/api/src/secrets.ts set signin.google
# (dev and test also read DIREX_GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET from here).
# Search Console uses a Workspace's own Google app first (set up on its SEO page), then a server
# app just for it (bun apps/api/src/secrets.ts set social_app.google_search_console, with
# client_id:client_secret on stdin), then this client. For this client, turn on the Search Console API:
# https://console.cloud.google.com/apis/library/searchconsole.googleapis.com
# Gmail Mailboxes use a Workspace's own Google app first (POST /api/w/{workspaceId}/credentials;
# see docs/mailboxes.md for the request),
# then the server's mailbox app, kept apart from sign-in (bun apps/api/src/secrets.ts set
# social_app.google, with client_id:client_secret on stdin), then this client. Set
# social_app.google before any Gmail Mailbox connects: a token works only with the app that
# issued it, so setting it later makes each Gmail Mailbox without a Workspace app reconnect once.
# DIREX_MICROSOFT_CLIENT_ID=
# Its client secret: bun apps/api/src/secrets.ts set signin.microsoft
# Which rules apply to model calls: self_host (the default) or cloud. Keys are never set here:
# bun apps/api/src/secrets.ts set provider.anthropic (also provider.openai, provider.google,
# provider.openrouter, smtp.url, auth.secret), with the value on stdin.
# DIREX_DEPLOYMENT=self_host
